<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dinuzulu kaCetshwayo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a>–<a href="/years/1913">1913</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dinuzulu kaCetshwayo was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> from 1884 to 1913, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetshwayo">Cetshwayo</a>. In 1884 he defeated his rival Zibhebhu with the help of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> volunteers, who in return took much of western Zululand as the Nieuwe Republiek. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> annexed Zululand he resisted in 1888, was convicted of treason and exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-helena">St Helena</a>, and returned in 1898. He was imprisoned again after the Bambatha rebellion of 1906.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dinuzulu-kacetshwayo.jpg" alt="Dinuzulu kaCetshwayo" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dinuzulu_Gewehr.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>His son <b>Dinuzulu</b> won Boer help against Zibhebhu at the price of land on which the Nieuwe Republiek was founded.</blockquote><a href="/empire/zulu-kingdom">Zulu Kingdom · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1884 Boers led by Lucas Meyer, among them the young Louis Botha, backed <b>Dinuzulu</b>, son of Cetshwayo, against Zibhebhu, and in return claimed a huge tract of Zulu land, where they proclaimed the Nieuwe Republiek with Lucas Meyer as president.</blockquote><a href="/state/nieuwe-republiek">Nieuwe Republiek</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Dinuzulu</b>, son of Cetshwayo, led resistance in 1888; he was tried for treason and exiled to St Helena.</blockquote><a href="/state/zululand-british-colony">Zululand (British colony)</a></li></ul></section>
